{:id :EACL-FORMAL-095
 :status :fixed
 :discovered-by :differential
 :seed-or-trace "eacl-rust/EACL-RS-001/semicolon-terminators"
 :minimized-fixture "fixture.edn"
 :impact :availability
 :affected-versions
 ["v8.0.0 commit a698b3bdf15e61be9bfd1324d7d7c67dc82176be"]
 :affected-backends [:shared]
 :root-cause
 "The Instaparse schema grammar was line-oriented: a relation or permission ended only at a line break, so SpiceDB's ';' statement terminators were a parse error and valid SpiceDB schemas that use them could not be written."
 :fix
 "Replace the grammar with a lexer and recursive-descent parser that follow SpiceDB v1.56.0's schemadsl: a statement ends at ';' or at a line end after a name, keyword, ')', '}' or '*' (SpiceDB's synthetic semicolon). A top-level declaration takes at most one terminator, a definition body accepts empty statements, and the last statement before '}' needs a terminator, as in SpiceDB."
 :closing-evidence
 ["eacl.spicedb.compatibility-corpus-test/semicolon-terminators-test"
  "eacl.spicedb.compatibility-corpus-test/spicedb-verdicts-test"]
 :notes
 "Found by the eacl-rust port (BUGS.md EACL-RS-001), verified against main a698b3bd and SpiceDB v1.56.0."}
